<div class="pdf-card"><span class="pdf-cat">Linux &amp; Systems</span><h3>firewalld</h3><p>Linux firewall management — zones, services, rich rules, and controlling traffic on the host.</p><a class="btn" href="/assets/pdfs/bbg-firewalld.pdf">Read the guide</a><div class="pdf-meta">8 pages · animated walkthrough</div></div>
<div class="pdf-card"><span class="pdf-cat">Linux &amp; Systems</span><h3>The Linux Kernel</h3><p>System calls, scheduling, and drivers — what the kernel does and how user space talks to it.</p><a class="btn" href="/assets/pdfs/bbg-kernel.pdf">Read the guide</a><div class="pdf-meta">8 pages · animated walkthrough</div></div>
<div class="pdf-card"><span class="pdf-cat">Linux &amp; Systems</span><h3>LVM &amp; RAID</h3><p>Logical volumes and redundant arrays — striping, mirroring, parity, and flexible Linux storage.</p><a class="btn" href="/assets/pdfs/bbg-lvm-raid.pdf">Read the guide</a><div class="pdf-meta">8 pages · animated walkthrough</div></div>
<div class="pdf-card"><span class="pdf-cat">Linux &amp; Systems</span><h3>Linux Memory Management</h3><p>Virtual memory, paging, and swap — how processes see memory and the kernel manages it.</p><a class="btn" href="/assets/pdfs/bbg-memory.pdf">Read the guide</a><div class="pdf-meta">8 pages · animated walkthrough</div></div>
<div class="pdf-card"><span class="pdf-cat">Linux &amp; Systems</span><h3>Network Commands</h3><p>ip, ss, dig, curl, tcpdump — the command-line toolkit for diagnosing networks.</p><a class="btn" href="/assets/pdfs/bbg-net-commands.pdf">Read the guide</a><div class="pdf-meta">8 pages · animated walkthrough</div></div>
<div class="pdf-card"><span class="pdf-cat">Linux &amp; Systems</span><h3>Linux Package Management</h3><p>apt, yum, and friends — repositories, dependencies, and keeping systems patched.</p><a class="btn" href="/assets/pdfs/bbg-packages.pdf">Read the guide</a><div class="pdf-meta">8 pages · animated walkthrough</div></div>
<div class="pdf-card"><span class="pdf-cat">Linux &amp; Systems</span><h3>Linux Performance Tools</h3><p>perf, flame graphs, and profilers — finding hotspots in CPU, memory, and I/O.</p><a class="btn" href="/assets/pdfs/bbg-perf.pdf">Read the guide</a><div class="pdf-meta">8 pages · animated walkthrough</div></div>
<div class="pdf-card"><span class="pdf-cat">Linux &amp; Systems</span><h3>Linux Permissions</h3><p>Users, groups, and mode bits — chmod, ownership, ACLs, and the principle of least privilege.</p><a class="btn" href="/assets/pdfs/bbg-permissions.pdf">Read the guide</a><div class="pdf-meta">8 pages · animated walkthrough</div></div>
<div class="pdf-card"><span class="pdf-cat">Linux &amp; Systems</span><h3>Linux Processes</h3><p>fork, exec, and signals — process lifecycle, PIDs, and how the kernel runs programs.</p><a class="btn" href="/assets/pdfs/bbg-processes.pdf">Read the guide</a><div class="pdf-meta">8 pages · animated walkthrough</div></div>
<div class="pdf-card"><span class="pdf-cat">Linux &amp; Systems</span><h3>SELinux</h3><p>Mandatory access control — contexts, policies, enforcing vs permissive, and taming denials.</p><a class="btn" href="/assets/pdfs/bbg-selinux.pdf">Read the guide</a><div class="pdf-meta">8 pages · animated walkthrough</div></div>
<div class="pdf-card"><span class="pdf-cat">Linux &amp; Systems</span><h3>SSH</h3><p>Secure shell — key pairs, agents, tunneling, and administering machines remotely and safely.</p><a class="btn" href="/assets/pdfs/bbg-ssh.pdf">Read the guide</a><div class="pdf-meta">8 pages · animated walkthrough</div></div>
